## k nearest neighbors

Under `"knn"`, every spot/cell has at least `k` neighbors, however far away
they are: for spots/cells near edges or gaps in the tissue, `"knn"` reaches
further to make up `k` neighbors.

::: {.grid-hex}
For a spot with six immediate neighbors on the grid, `k = 6` yields the same
neighborhood as the default radius. For other values of `k`, spots at the same
distance are chosen arbitrarily.
:::

::: {.grid-square}
Away from edges, `k = 4` and `k = 8` give the same neighbors as radii of
9.6 µm and 12 µm, but `k = 6` has to choose between the four diagonals, so it
chooses arbitrarily.
:::

::: {.lang-r .grid-hex}

::: {.cell layout-ncol="3"}

